Interpretation and hardware boundary
------------------------------------
The free scene has neq=0 and a real base_free joint. The live simulator is
controlled only through the canonical 20 motor targets; the acceptance tools
also prove one HumanoidSimulation/MjData instance across replay and settling.
No-fall is not equivalent to passing contact safety or pose fidelity.

The MuJoCo inertial/contact model remains provisional. The legacy WebSocket is
a 10 Hz command-only output: there is no real encoder/IMU/foot-load feedback,
execution acknowledgement, onboard watchdog or hardware E-stop in this repo.
These simulation results are not a physical-robot safety certificate.
